<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent) Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	19.95	    -0.95	   19.85     19.99</p>
<p>91-Day	19.64	    -1.62	   19.59     19.65</p>
<p>181-Day     20.56	    -0.92	   20.49     20.70</p>
<p>364-Day     21.16</p>
<p>Last week the 343-day paper was assigned at 22.08 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   5.19 bln pesos     6.49</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   6.50 bln pesos     8.13</p>
<p>181-Day     800 million pesos   3.05 bln pesos     3.81</p>
<p>364-Day     600 million pesos   1.83 bln pesos     3.05</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 5.53 on demand of 16.57 billion pesos compared with 4.78 the week before, on demand of 14.35 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    4 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    1 basis points</p>
<p>    181-Day			  14 basis points</p>
<p>    364-Day			  15 basis points</p>
<p>((--Caroline Brothers, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
